        "synthesis": {
          "title": "Cracks in the Islamic Republic, v30 - market strike rumor fades into managed freeze",
          "summary": "The thirtieth pass follows the immediate Bazaar/Ferdowsi/Aladdin question after the 27-29 April protest and partial closure. It does not find a verified renewed Saturday strike cluster: Exa turns up price and market-management reports rather than source-near closure reporting, and xPool is sparse even with broad terms. That lowers the probability of a visible May 2 Bazaar strike, but it is not normalization. The market crack has shifted into administrative freeze and price shock. The stock market remains formally stopped until at least 14 Ordibehesht, and reopening is described as conditional on requirements and information transparency. Mobile-market reporting says prices rose 30-40%, import registration stopped, customs costs rose, and consumers are shifting to repair instead of replacement. FX discourse remains unstable after the 180k-toman dollar record, with Fararu framing dollar/gold movement as doubt rather than clear stabilization. Net: collective merchant action appears contained for now, but the regime is buying quiet through halted trading, conditional reopening, price enforcement, and thin information flow while household and trader price reality keeps worsening.",
